cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "CuHalide Atlas is currently a prepublication review resource, not a formally deposited public dataset. For living-atlas results shared during review, report the access date and Current Curated revision. Archived scientific snapshot 3.0.2 remains the immutable historical baseline for exact reproduction."
title: "CuHalide Atlas"
version: "Current Curated rev.8 (prepublication review)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "CuHalide Atlas Project"
url: "https://cuhalide-atlas-v3.vercel.app/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zion0321/CuHalide-Atlas"
abstract: >-
  Prepublication review resource for an evidence-grounded, structure-resolved
  knowledge base covering organic-containing Cu(I) chlorides, bromides and
  iodides. Current Curated rev.8 is reviewed through 2026-08-19, retains the
  complete rev.7 hostile structure-truth audit, and adds a narrow
  primary-source-reverified correction set for structure-grain motif,
  dimensionality and chemical-identity mapping. Reported composition, local
  Cu-X motif and global connectivity dimensionality remain separated at the
  appropriate evidence grain. Archived scientific snapshot 3.0.2 is retained
  as an immutable historical baseline. Direct-link review access is
  query-and-view; search-engine indexing, bulk normalized exports, exact stored
  publisher abstracts, primary PDF/SI/CIF files and internal curation/audit
  artifacts remain outside the public release boundary. No permanent DOI,
  blanket license or formal public-release date is asserted until owner approval.
keywords:
  - copper(I) halide
  - Cu(I)-I
  - copper iodide
  - crystallography
  - luminescence
  - self-trapped exciton
  - scientific knowledge portal
  - retrieval-augmented generation
